    {
      "id": "sce-pmf-three-stages-q-050fb8c2",
      "type": "short",
      "stem": "Why does a startup that has not reached product-market fit focus on validated learning and pivots?",
      "options": [],
      "answer": "",
      "accept": [],
      "explanation": "",
      "model_answer_md": "Before product-market fit, the stage questions are whether the problem is worth solving and whether people want what has been built. The deck sets the focus as **validated learning**, the experiments as **pivots** and the terrain as **qualitative**.\n\nThis fits the earlier message that 66% drastically change their original plans: the work is to find the path to a plan that works.",
