    {
      "id": "sce-pmf-three-stages-q-253bc078",
      "type": "long",
      "stem": "Explain the three stages of a startup and how the focus, experiments and terrain change before and after product-market fit.",
      "options": [],
      "answer": "",
      "accept": [],
      "explanation": "",
      "model_answer_md": "The deck describes a startup as moving through **three stages**: Problem/Solution Fit (Stage 1), Product/Market Fit (Stage 2) and Scale (Stage 3).\n\n**Stage questions.**\n- Problem/Solution Fit: do I have a problem worth solving?\n- Product/Market Fit: have I built something people want?\n- Scale: how do I accelerate growth?\n\n**Before Product/Market Fit** (the first two stages): the **focus** is validated learning, the **experiments** are pivots, and the **terrain** is qualitative.\n\n**After Product/Market Fit** (Scale): the **focus** is growth, the **experiments** are optimizations, and the **terrain** is quantitative.\n\nThe deck also says product-market fit is the first thing that matters and should be found before the money runs out, so the first two stages decide whether the third is possible.\n\nIn conclusion, early work is about learning and changing direction; later work is about measured growth.",
